{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TD4r4kbzo4fdheMo9Z8oyq","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Fix Plan\n     2→\n     3→## Priority: Polish (tasks 1-9)\n     4→\n     5→- [ ] 1. Capture more regression tests (enum match, struct mutation, while+break, nested if-else, multi-arg call, substring)\n     6→- [ ] 2. Remove [BC] debug print from std-llvm (gate behind env var)\n     7→- [ ] 3. Audit std-llvm silent fallbacks (replace LLVMConstInt/LLVMGetUndef with eprintln+null)\n     8→- [ ] 4. Add example.fg + expected.out to all feature directories\n     9→- [ ] 5. Short-circuit && / || lowering (cond_br + phi instead of eager mul/add)\n    10→- [ ] 6. emit_stmt_as_value coverage audit\n    11→- [ ] 7. Exhaustive match audit (grep for _ -> {} and _ -> ok_stmt)\n    12→- [ ] 8. Remove [char_at] stderr debug noise from runtime.c\n    13→- [ ] 9. Clean up TECH_DEBT.md (collapse fixed items, update stale ones)\n    14→\n    15→## Priority: Phase A features (tasks 10-15)\n    16→\n    17→For each feature: create features/<name>/ dir, add parser.fg + codegen.fg + example.fg + expected.out, then REFACTOR bootstrap source to USE the new feature. Verify with `make -C bootstrap test`.\n    18→\n    19→- [ ] 10. `for` loops + ranges (for i in 0..n { })\n    20→- [ ] 11. String templates (`hello ${name}`)\n    21→- [ ] 12. Pipe operator (expr |> fn)\n    22→- [ ] 13. `const` bindings\n    23→- [ ] 14. Hex/bin/oct numeric literals (0xFF, 0b1010, 0o755)\n    24→- [ ] 15. `and`/`or`/`not` keyword operators\n    25→\n    26→## Priority: More std-llvm hardening (tasks 16-18)\n    27→\n    28→- [ ] 16. forge_llvm_build_call arg-count / arg-type validation (check args match fn_type params, refuse loudly on mismatch)\n    29→- [ ] 17. forge_llvm_build_load type compatibility (warn when load ty differs from LLVMGetAllocatedType for alloca destinations)\n    30→- [ ] 18. Match expression type unification (emit_match_expr_arms should verify all arms produce the same type, not just use the first)\n    31→\n    32→## When all tasks are done\n    33→\n    34→Set EXIT_SIGNAL: true in your RALPH_STATUS block.\n    35→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99531a4f-114c-49ff-a929-dced21bdd83f","uuid":"96ab2e52-40b9-42e6-877b-105d256d6201","timestamp":"2026-04-09T09:47:14.277Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/.ralph/fix_plan.md","content":"# Fix Plan\n\n## Priority: Polish (tasks 1-9)\n\n- [ ] 1. Capture more regression tests (enum match, struct mutation, while+break, nested if-else, multi-arg call, substring)\n- [ ] 2. Remove [BC] debug print from std-llvm (gate behind env var)\n- [ ] 3. Audit std-llvm silent fallbacks (replace LLVMConstInt/LLVMGetUndef with eprintln+null)\n- [ ] 4. Add example.fg + expected.out to all feature directories\n- [ ] 5. Short-circuit && / || lowering (cond_br + phi instead of eager mul/add)\n- [ ] 6. emit_stmt_as_value coverage audit\n- [ ] 7. Exhaustive match audit (grep for _ -> {} and _ -> ok_stmt)\n- [ ] 8. Remove [char_at] stderr debug noise from runtime.c\n- [ ] 9. Clean up TECH_DEBT.md (collapse fixed items, update stale ones)\n\n## Priority: Phase A features (tasks 10-15)\n\nFor each feature: create features/<name>/ dir, add parser.fg + codegen.fg + example.fg + expected.out, then REFACTOR bootstrap source to USE the new feature. Verify with `make -C bootstrap test`.\n\n- [ ] 10. `for` loops + ranges (for i in 0..n { })\n- [ ] 11. String templates (`hello ${name}`)\n- [ ] 12. Pipe operator (expr |> fn)\n- [ ] 13. `const` bindings\n- [ ] 14. Hex/bin/oct numeric literals (0xFF, 0b1010, 0o755)\n- [ ] 15. `and`/`or`/`not` keyword operators\n\n## Priority: More std-llvm hardening (tasks 16-18)\n\n- [ ] 16. forge_llvm_build_call arg-count / arg-type validation (check args match fn_type params, refuse loudly on mismatch)\n- [ ] 17. forge_llvm_build_load type compatibility (warn when load ty differs from LLVMGetAllocatedType for alloca destinations)\n- [ ] 18. Match expression type unification (emit_match_expr_arms should verify all arms produce the same type, not just use the first)\n\n## When all tasks are done\n\nSet EXIT_SIGNAL: true in your RALPH_STATUS block.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}}}
