{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DzqpZCTVC988hkTzksevhn","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Feature Parity: Bootstrap vs Forge Language\n     2→\n     3→Complete inventory. Every feature of the Forge language is listed\n     4→below with its bootstrap status. Source of truth: `forge lang --llm`\n     5→and `forge features` (67 features, 62 stable).\n     6→\n     7→Status key:\n     8→  ✅ = implemented in bootstrap\n     9→  🔲 = not yet implemented\n    10→  ⬜ = not applicable to bootstrap (domain-specific / runtime-only)\n    11→\n    12→---\n    13→\n    14→## Variables & Bindings\n    15→\n    16→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n    17→|---|---|---|---|\n    18→| let binding | `let x = 1` | ✅ | |\n    19→| mut binding | `mut y = 2` | ✅ | |\n    20→| const binding | `const Z = 3` | 🔲 | |\n    21→| type annotation | `let x: int = 42` | ✅ | optional, defaults to i64 |\n    22→| immutability enforcement | `x = 2` errors if `let` | 🔲 | bootstrap allows mutation on let |\n    23→| field mutability | `type T = { mut x: int }` | ✅ | parsed, not enforced |\n    24→| shorthand fields | `Foo { name }` = `Foo { name: name }` | ✅ | |\n    25→\n    26→## Primitive Types\n    27→\n    28→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n    29→|---|---|---|---|\n    30→| int (i64) | `42`, `-1`, `1_000_000` | ✅ | |\n    31→| float (f64) | `3.14`, `1.0e10` | 🔲 | parsed but not codegen'd |\n    32→| string | `\"hello\"` | ✅ | raw cstr in bootstrap |\n    33→| bool | `true`, `false` | ✅ | |\n    34→| null | `null` | ✅ | = i64 0 |\n    35→| hex/bin/oct literals | `0xFF`, `0b1010`, `0o755` | 🔲 | |\n    36→| numeric underscores | `1_000_000` | 🔲 | |\n    37→\n    38→## Functions\n    39→\n    40→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n    41→|---|---|---|---|\n    42→| fn declaration | `fn name(params) -> type { body }` | ✅ | |\n    43→| return | `return expr` | ✅ | |\n    44→| implicit return | last expression is return value | ✅ | |\n    45→| extern fn | `extern fn name(params) -> type` | ✅ | C ABI |\n    46→| fn types | `fn(A, B) -> R` | 🔲 | |\n    47→| closures / lambdas | `(x) -> x * 2` | 🔲 | **high priority** |\n    48→| `it` parameter | `.method(it * 2)` | 🔲 | needs closures |\n    49→| generics | `fn name<T>(x: T) -> T` | 🔲 | **high priority** |\n    50→| generic constraints | `fn name<T: Trait>(x: T)` | 🔲 | needs generics + traits |\n    51→\n    52→## Structs & Types\n    53→\n    54→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n    55→|---|---|---|---|\n    56→| type declaration | `type T = { fields }` | ✅ | |\n    57→| struct literal | `Foo { x: 1, y: 2 }` | ✅ | |\n    58→| field access | `obj.field` | ✅ | |\n    59→| field assign | `obj.field = val` | ✅ | |\n    60→| `with` expression | `obj with { field: val }` | 🔲 | functional update |\n    61→| traits | `trait Name { fn method(self) }` | 🔲 | **high priority** |\n    62→| impl for trait | `impl Trait for Type { }` | 🔲 | needs traits |\n    63→| impl block | `impl Type { fn method(self) }` | ✅ | desugars to Type__method |\n    64→\n    65→## Enums & Pattern Matching\n    66→\n    67→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n    68→|---|---|---|---|\n    69→| enum declaration | `enum Name { A, B(x: int) }` | ✅ | |\n    70→| enum constructor | `Name.Variant(args)` | ✅ | |\n    71→| match statement | `match expr { .A -> ... }` | ✅ | |\n    72→| match expression | `let x = match expr { ... }` | ✅ | |\n    73→| wildcard pattern | `_ -> ...` | ✅ | |\n    74→| variant binding | `.A(x, y) -> use(x)` | ✅ | |\n    75→| nested patterns | `.A(.Inner(x), y) -> ...` | 🔲 | |\n    76→| match guards | `pattern if guard -> body` | 🔲 | |\n    77→| match tables | `match expr table { ... }` | 🔲 | |\n    78→| `is` keyword | `value is Pattern` | 🔲 | |\n    79→| contextual resolution | `let x: Enum = .variant` | 🔲 | |\n    80→\n    81→## Control Flow\n    82→\n    83→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n    84→|---|---|---|---|\n    85→| if / else | `if cond { } else { }` | ✅ | stmt + expr form |\n    86→| else if | `if a { } else if b { }` | ✅ | |\n    87→| while | `while cond { body }` | ✅ | |\n    88→| for-in | `for x in collection { }` | 🔲 | **high priority** |\n    89→| for-range | `for i in 0..10 { }` | 🔲 | needs ranges |\n    90→| break / continue | `break`, `continue` | ✅ | scoped via Ctx.loops |\n    91→| expression blocks | `{ stmts; last_expr }` | ✅ | |\n    92→| defer | `defer cleanup()` | 🔲 | |\n    93→\n    94→## Operators\n    95→\n    96→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n    97→|---|---|---|---|\n    98→| arithmetic | `+`, `-`, `*`, `/` | ✅ | |\n    99→| comparison | `==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` | ✅ | |\n   100→| logical | `&&`, `||` | ✅ | **eager, not short-circuit** |\n   101→| logical keywords | `and`, `or`, `not` | 🔲 | |\n   102→| unary | `-x`, `!x` | ✅ | |\n   103→| bitwise | `&`, `|`, `^`, `<<`, `>>`, `~` | 🔲 | |\n   104→| pipe | `expr |> fn` | 🔲 | |\n   105→| ranges | `start..end`, `start..=end` | 🔲 | |\n   106→| type operators | `without`, `only`, `partial` | 🔲 | |\n   107→\n   108→## Strings\n   109→\n   110→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n   111→|---|---|---|---|\n   112→| string literals | `\"hello\"` | ✅ | |\n   113→| string concat | `a + b` | ✅ | |\n   114→| string indexing | `s[i]` | ✅ | returns 1-char string |\n   115→| `.length` | `s.length` | ✅ | via strlen |\n   116→| `.substring` | `s.substring(start, end)` | ✅ | |\n   117→| string templates | `` `hello ${name}` `` | 🔲 | **high priority** |\n   118→| tagged templates | `` tag`template` `` | 🔲 | needs templates |\n   119→| `.split`, `.trim`, etc. | `s.split(sep)` | 🔲 | |\n   120→| `.contains`, `.starts_with` | `s.contains(sub)` | 🔲 | |\n   121→| `.replace`, `.upper`, `.lower` | `s.replace(a, b)` | 🔲 | |\n   122→| `char_code(s)` | `char_code(\"A\")` | 🔲 | |\n   123→\n   124→## Null Safety\n   125→\n   126→| Feature | Forge syntax | Bootstrap | Notes |\n   127→|---