{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RGkfPQEKR22Wd4E5Q2H9dn","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Summary: Bootstrap Compiler Syntax Exploration\n\n### 1. Which features have example.fg files\n\nOnly **1 feature** has an example.fg file:\n- `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/example.fg`\n\nAll other features only have `mod.fg`, `parser.fg`, and (sometimes) `codegen.fg` files, but no example.fg.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Enum Syntax (enum_decl)\n\nFrom `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/example.fg`:\n\n```\nenum Shape {\n    Circle(radius: int)\n    Square(side: int)\n    Unknown\n}\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- Variant names are capitalized\n- Payloads use named fields in parentheses: `VariantName(field: type, ...)`\n- Nullary (no-payload) variants like `Unknown` are supported\n- Variants are comma-separated (or newline-separated)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Match Syntax (match)\n\nFrom the example and `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/example.fg`:\n\n```\nmatch s {\n    .Circle(r) -> r * r * 3\n    .Square(side) -> side * side\n    .Unknown -> 0\n}\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- Match expression: `match <subject> { <arms> }`\n- Arms use dot notation: `.VariantName(bindings)` or `.VariantName` (nullary)\n- Wildcard pattern: `_` (shown in codegen but not example)\n- Arrow syntax: `pattern -> expression`\n- Arms are comma-separated\n- Match can be both **statement** and **expression**\n\n---\n\n### 4. Struct Mutation Syntax (struct_decl / impl_decl)\n\nFrom `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/struct_decl/codegen.fg`:\n\n```\nemit_struct_lit(ctx, env, name, inits)\n```\n\nThe codegen shows:\n- Struct literals are constructed via field initialization list\n- Fields are filled: `forge_llvm_build_struct_gep2(ctx.builder, st_ty, buf, idx, \"fld_ptr\")`\n- Pattern: `fill_struct_fields` recursively fills fields using `FieldInitList`\n\nHowever, **no mutation/assignment syntax is demonstrated** in the example or codegen files. The syntax appears to be immutable (functional) style.\n\n---\n\n### 5. While + Break Syntax (while_stmt)\n\nFrom `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/while_stmt/codegen.fg`:\n\n```\nwhile cond { body }\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- While loop: `while <condition> { <body> }`\n- Codegen shows:\n  - Loop stack frame: `LoopStack.Frame(cond_bb, exit_bb, ctx.loops)`\n  - Break/continue supported via scoped loop context\n  - Three basic blocks: condition, body, exit\n  - Condition is converted to i1 via `forge_llvm_build_icmp`\n\n**Note:** The codegen mentions break/continue support via loop stack, but no explicit syntax example is shown.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Existing Feature Examples Demonstrated\n\nThe single `match/example.fg` demonstrates:\n- Enum declaration with payload and nullary variants\n- Pattern matching with and without bindings\n- Match as expression (with return value)\n- Function declaration and main entry point\n- Function calls and arithmetic expressions\n- String conversion and println\n\nAll features with codegen support:\n- `fn_decl` - function body emission with parameter binding\n- `enum_decl` - enum constructor emission (tagged unions)\n- `struct_decl` - struct literal construction and field filling\n- `match` - match expression/statement emission\n- `if_stmt` - conditional branching\n- `while_stmt` - loop with break/continue support via scoped stack\n- `let_stmt` - variable binding with LLVM alloca/store\n- `return_stmt` - function returns\n\n---\n\n### File Locations Reference\n\n- Match example: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/example.fg`\n- Codegen implementations: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/{feature}/codegen.fg`\n- Parser implementations: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/{feature}/parser.fg`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99531a4f-114c-49ff-a929-dced21bdd83f","uuid":"8aa455e9-3d41-4502-96fc-7fb4588d2f99","timestamp":"2026-04-09T09:49:14.772Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Quick exploration: In /Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/, look at each feature's example.fg file (if it exists) and codegen.fg to understand the syntax the bootstrap compiler supports. I need to know:\n1. Which features have example.fg files already\n2. What enum syntax looks like (enum_decl)\n3. What match syntax looks like (match)\n4. What struct mutation syntax looks like (struct_decl / impl_decl)\n5. What while+break syntax looks like (while_stmt)\n6. What the existing feature examples demonstrate\n\nRead the example.fg files and a few lines from the codegen.fg files to understand the supported syntax.","agentId":"a667ff2a229955548","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Summary: Bootstrap Compiler Syntax Exploration\n\n### 1. Which features have example.fg files\n\nOnly **1 feature** has an example.fg file:\n- `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/example.fg`\n\nAll other features only have `mod.fg`, `parser.fg`, and (sometimes) `codegen.fg` files, but no example.fg.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Enum Syntax (enum_decl)\n\nFrom `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/example.fg`:\n\n```\nenum Shape {\n    Circle(radius: int)\n    Square(side: int)\n    Unknown\n}\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- Variant names are capitalized\n- Payloads use named fields in parentheses: `VariantName(field: type, ...)`\n- Nullary (no-payload) variants like `Unknown` are supported\n- Variants are comma-separated (or newline-separated)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Match Syntax (match)\n\nFrom the example and `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/example.fg`:\n\n```\nmatch s {\n    .Circle(r) -> r * r * 3\n    .Square(side) -> side * side\n    .Unknown -> 0\n}\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- Match expression: `match <subject> { <arms> }`\n- Arms use dot notation: `.VariantName(bindings)` or `.VariantName` (nullary)\n- Wildcard pattern: `_` (shown in codegen but not example)\n- Arrow syntax: `pattern -> expression`\n- Arms are comma-separated\n- Match can be both **statement** and **expression**\n\n---\n\n### 4. Struct Mutation Syntax (struct_decl / impl_decl)\n\nFrom `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/struct_decl/codegen.fg`:\n\n```\nemit_struct_lit(ctx, env, name, inits)\n```\n\nThe codegen shows:\n- Struct literals are constructed via field initialization list\n- Fields are filled: `forge_llvm_build_struct_gep2(ctx.builder, st_ty, buf, idx, \"fld_ptr\")`\n- Pattern: `fill_struct_fields` recursively fills fields using `FieldInitList`\n\nHowever, **no mutation/assignment syntax is demonstrated** in the example or codegen files. The syntax appears to be immutable (functional) style.\n\n---\n\n### 5. While + Break Syntax (while_stmt)\n\nFrom `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/while_stmt/codegen.fg`:\n\n```\nwhile cond { body }\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- While loop: `while <condition> { <body> }`\n- Codegen shows:\n  - Loop stack frame: `LoopStack.Frame(cond_bb, exit_bb, ctx.loops)`\n  - Break/continue supported via scoped loop context\n  - Three basic blocks: condition, body, exit\n  - Condition is converted to i1 via `forge_llvm_build_icmp`\n\n**Note:** The codegen mentions break/continue support via loop stack, but no explicit syntax example is shown.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Existing Feature Examples Demonstrated\n\nThe single `match/example.fg` demonstrates:\n- Enum declaration with payload and nullary variants\n- Pattern matching with and without bindings\n- Match as expression (with return value)\n- Function declaration and main entry point\n- Function calls and arithmetic expressions\n- String conversion and println\n\nAll features with codegen support:\n- `fn_decl` - function body emission with parameter binding\n- `enum_decl` - enum constructor emission (tagged unions)\n- `struct_decl` - struct literal construction and field filling\n- `match` - match expression/statement emission\n- `if_stmt` - conditional branching\n- `while_stmt` - loop with break/continue support via scoped stack\n- `let_stmt` - variable binding with LLVM alloca/store\n- `return_stmt` - function returns\n\n---\n\n### File Locations Reference\n\n- Match example: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/example.fg`\n- Codegen implementations: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/{feature}/codegen.fg`\n- Parser implementations: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/{feature}/parser.fg`"}],"totalDurationMs":52294,"totalTokens":127290,"totalToolUseCount":18,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":125738,"output_tokens":1199,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":350},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
