{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019rchxkM1MxA9J3DF9H68CN","type":"tool_result","content":"93:  --regress            Compile + run every regress/*.fg with bs2 and\n94-                       compare stdout against the matching .out file.\n95-                       Exit non-zero on any mismatch. Run before commit.\n96:  --regress-add <name> <file.fg>\n97-                       Capture <file.fg> as a regression test under\n98-                       regress/<name>.fg, with bs2's current stdout\n99-                       saved as regress/<name>.out.\n100:  --regress-list       List all captured regression tests.\n101-\n102-HEAP / MEMORY DEBUGGING\n103-  --asan   <file.fg>   Run bs2_asan on <file.fg>. AddressSanitizer\n104-                       reports the exact alloc/use-after-free site.\n105-                       Builds bs2_asan if missing.\n106-  --malloc-trace <file.fg>\n107-                       Run bs2 under MallocStackLogging + DYLD malloc\n108-                       guard. Crash dumps include the alloc backtrace.\n109-  --bisect-lines <file.fg>\n110-                       Binary-search the line count of <file.fg> to find\n111-                       the smallest prefix that still makes bs2 crash.\n112-                       Useful for isolating heap-corruption triggers.\n113-\n114-ENVIRONMENT\n115-  LLVM_PREFIX  Override the LLVM 19 install prefix.\n116-               Default: /opt/homebrew/opt/llvm@19\n117-\n118-EXAMPLES\n119-  diagnose.sh --build               # rebuild stage1 from rust + run tests\n120-  diagnose.sh --build-bs2           # build the self-compiled bs2\n--\n124:  diagnose.sh --regress             # run regression suite\n125:  diagnose.sh --regress-add hello /tmp/hello.fg\n126-EOF\n127-}\n128-\n129-# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n130-# Build helpers\n131-# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n132-\n133-ensure_host_compiler() {\n134-