{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CH4vbLNm1auL9tbFPqJC5k","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile a comprehensive report of all the syntax patterns I found:\n\n## Bootstrap Compiler Syntax Patterns Report\n\nBased on my exploration of the Forge bootstrap compiler source code (written in Forge itself), here are the **real usage patterns** from the actual codebase:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Break in While Loops**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/main.fg` (lines 64-92)\n\n```forge\nwhile i < n {\n    if source[i] == \"\\n\" {\n        i = i + 1\n        break\n    }\n    i = i + 1\n}\n```\n\nAlso used in the parser preprocessing loop to exit the module name extraction loop.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Struct Field Mutation (Field Assignment)**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/parse/mod.fg` (lines 580-648, 739-741)\n\n```forge\nlet saved = self.allow_struct_lit\nself.allow_struct_lit = false\nlet condition = self.parse_expression()\nself.allow_struct_lit = saved\n```\n\nAnd:\n```forge\nself.current_kind = kind\nself.current_lexeme = lexeme\n```\n\nThe pattern shows `self.field = value` for mutation inside functions that take `self` (impl methods).\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Nested If-Else Chains**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/if_stmt/parser.fg` (lines 23-30)\n\n```forge\nif self.check(\"kw_else\") {\n    self.advance()\n    let else_branch = self.parse_statement()\n    if else_branch == null { return null }\n    return Stmt.If(condition!, then_branch!, else_branch)\n}\n\nStmt.If(condition!, then_branch!, null)\n```\n\nAnd from `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/if_stmt/parser.fg` (lines 46-64):\n\n```forge\nif !self.check(\"kw_else\") {\n    return Expr.IfExpr(condition!, then_branch!, Expr.Number(\"0\"))\n}\nself.advance()\nif self.check(\"kw_if\") {\n    let else_branch = self.parse_if_expression()\n    if else_branch == null { return null }\n    return Expr.IfExpr(condition!, then_branch!, else_branch!)\n}\nif self.check(\"left_brace\") {\n    let else_branch = self.parse_block_expression()\n    if else_branch == null { return null }\n    return Expr.IfExpr(condition!, then_branch!, else_branch!)\n}\nlet else_branch = self.parse_expression()\n```\n\nReal `else if` chains work by chaining if-expressions through recursion.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Multi-Arg Function Calls (3+ Parameters)**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/codegen/mod.fg` (lines 50-102)\n\n```forge\nlet puts_type = forge_llvm_function_type(forge_llvm_int32_type(lc), puts_param_arr, 1, 0)\n```\n\nAnd the crucial pattern:\n```forge\nlet memcpy_param_arr = forge_llvm_type_array_new(3)\nforge_llvm_type_array_set(memcpy_param_arr, 0, pt)\nforge_llvm_type_array_set(memcpy_param_arr, 1, pt)\nforge_llvm_type_array_set(memcpy_param_arr, 2, i64t)\nlet memcpy_type = forge_llvm_function_type(pt, memcpy_param_arr, 3, 0)\n```\n\nAnd:\n```forge\nlet snprintf_type = forge_llvm_function_type(forge_llvm_int32_type(lc), snprintf_param_arr, 3, 1)\n```\n\nFunctions frequently called with 4+ arguments.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Substring Method Calls**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/main.fg` (lines 67, 94, 151)\n\n```forge\nreturn path.substring(0, i)\n\nlet line = source.substring(line_start, i)\n\nline.substring(name_start, j)\n```\n\nAnd from core/cg.fg:\n```forge\nlet head = ty.substring(0, 5)\nty.substring(5, ty.length)\n```\n\nPattern: `string.substring(start_index, end_index)` - used extensively for string slicing.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Enum Match Patterns**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/codegen.fg` (lines 34-67)\n\n```forge\nmatch arms {\n    .End -> {\n        if forge_llvm_block_has_terminator(ctx.builder) == 0 {\n            forge_llvm_build_br(ctx.builder, merge_bb)\n        }\n        EmitResult { value: null_ptr_val(), ty: \"i64\", had_error: false, error_message: \"\" }\n    }\n    .Node(pattern, body, next) -> {\n        let arm_bb = new_bb(ctx, \"march_arm\")\n        let next_bb = new_bb(ctx, \"march_next\")\n        match pattern {\n            .Wildcard -> forge_llvm_build_br(ctx.builder, arm_bb)\n            .Variant(vname, _) -> {\n                let v = variant_lookup(variants, vname)\n                if !v.found { return err_emit(\"pattern references unknown variant `\" + vname + \"`\") }\n                let want_tag = const_i8(ctx, v.tag)\n                let cmp = forge_llvm_build_icmp(ctx.builder, 32, tag_val, want_tag, \"tag_eq\")\n                forge_llvm_build_cond_br(ctx.builder, cmp, arm_bb, next_bb)\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAnd from parse/mod.fg (lines 61-71):\n```forge\nfn expr_is_ident(e: Expr) -> bool {\n    match e {\n        .Ident(_) -> true\n        _ -> false\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- `.VariantName` syntax for pattern matching\n- `.VariantName(arg1, arg2)` for capturing payloads\n- `_` as wildcard\n- `.End` and `.Node(...)` for linked-list style ADTs\n- Nested `match` statements inside match arms\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Real Usage\n\nThe bootstrap compiler demonstrates:\n\n1. **break**: Used in preprocessing loop to exit when newline found\n2. **Field mutation**: `parser.field = value` inside impl methods, saving/restoring parser state\n3. **Nested if-else**: Multiple sequential `if` checks, with early `return`, creating chains\n4. **Multi-arg calls**: Heavy use of 3-4 arg functions like `forge_llvm_function_type()`, `forge_llvm_build_*()`, and `forge_llvm_type_array_set()`\n5. **substring**: Widely used for string slicing, always with `(start, end)` indices\n6. **Enum match**: Both simple variants (`.End`, `.Node`) and parameterized variants (`.Variant(name, params)`) with nested matching and wildcards"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99531a4f-114c-49ff-a929-dced21bdd83f","uuid":"51849fb5-ad76-4800-8676-cf1fdd6201cd","timestamp":"2026-04-09T09:50:27.721Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Quick exploration in /Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/. I need to verify what syntax patterns the bootstrap compiler supports by looking at its own source code for real examples. Look at:\n\n1. How break is used in while loops - search for \"break\" usage\n2. How structs with mutation are used - search for field assignment like \"x.field = val\" \n3. How nested if-else chains work - find examples of if/else if/else patterns\n4. How multi-arg function calls work - find functions with 3+ parameters\n5. How substring is called - search for \".substring\" usage\n6. How enum match works in the source code (not just the example)\n\nFocus on real usage patterns from the bootstrap source itself. Check 3-4 files to see real syntax.","agentId":"a704ac52613d92326","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile a comprehensive report of all the syntax patterns I found:\n\n## Bootstrap Compiler Syntax Patterns Report\n\nBased on my exploration of the Forge bootstrap compiler source code (written in Forge itself), here are the **real usage patterns** from the actual codebase:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Break in While Loops**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/main.fg` (lines 64-92)\n\n```forge\nwhile i < n {\n    if source[i] == \"\\n\" {\n        i = i + 1\n        break\n    }\n    i = i + 1\n}\n```\n\nAlso used in the parser preprocessing loop to exit the module name extraction loop.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Struct Field Mutation (Field Assignment)**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/parse/mod.fg` (lines 580-648, 739-741)\n\n```forge\nlet saved = self.allow_struct_lit\nself.allow_struct_lit = false\nlet condition = self.parse_expression()\nself.allow_struct_lit = saved\n```\n\nAnd:\n```forge\nself.current_kind = kind\nself.current_lexeme = lexeme\n```\n\nThe pattern shows `self.field = value` for mutation inside functions that take `self` (impl methods).\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Nested If-Else Chains**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/if_stmt/parser.fg` (lines 23-30)\n\n```forge\nif self.check(\"kw_else\") {\n    self.advance()\n    let else_branch = self.parse_statement()\n    if else_branch == null { return null }\n    return Stmt.If(condition!, then_branch!, else_branch)\n}\n\nStmt.If(condition!, then_branch!, null)\n```\n\nAnd from `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/if_stmt/parser.fg` (lines 46-64):\n\n```forge\nif !self.check(\"kw_else\") {\n    return Expr.IfExpr(condition!, then_branch!, Expr.Number(\"0\"))\n}\nself.advance()\nif self.check(\"kw_if\") {\n    let else_branch = self.parse_if_expression()\n    if else_branch == null { return null }\n    return Expr.IfExpr(condition!, then_branch!, else_branch!)\n}\nif self.check(\"left_brace\") {\n    let else_branch = self.parse_block_expression()\n    if else_branch == null { return null }\n    return Expr.IfExpr(condition!, then_branch!, else_branch!)\n}\nlet else_branch = self.parse_expression()\n```\n\nReal `else if` chains work by chaining if-expressions through recursion.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Multi-Arg Function Calls (3+ Parameters)**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/codegen/mod.fg` (lines 50-102)\n\n```forge\nlet puts_type = forge_llvm_function_type(forge_llvm_int32_type(lc), puts_param_arr, 1, 0)\n```\n\nAnd the crucial pattern:\n```forge\nlet memcpy_param_arr = forge_llvm_type_array_new(3)\nforge_llvm_type_array_set(memcpy_param_arr, 0, pt)\nforge_llvm_type_array_set(memcpy_param_arr, 1, pt)\nforge_llvm_type_array_set(memcpy_param_arr, 2, i64t)\nlet memcpy_type = forge_llvm_function_type(pt, memcpy_param_arr, 3, 0)\n```\n\nAnd:\n```forge\nlet snprintf_type = forge_llvm_function_type(forge_llvm_int32_type(lc), snprintf_param_arr, 3, 1)\n```\n\nFunctions frequently called with 4+ arguments.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Substring Method Calls**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/main.fg` (lines 67, 94, 151)\n\n```forge\nreturn path.substring(0, i)\n\nlet line = source.substring(line_start, i)\n\nline.substring(name_start, j)\n```\n\nAnd from core/cg.fg:\n```forge\nlet head = ty.substring(0, 5)\nty.substring(5, ty.length)\n```\n\nPattern: `string.substring(start_index, end_index)` - used extensively for string slicing.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Enum Match Patterns**\n\n**File**: `/Users/tristan/projects/tristanMatthias/forge-crafting-intepreters/bootstrap/src/features/match/codegen.fg` (lines 34-67)\n\n```forge\nmatch arms {\n    .End -> {\n        if forge_llvm_block_has_terminator(ctx.builder) == 0 {\n            forge_llvm_build_br(ctx.builder, merge_bb)\n        }\n        EmitResult { value: null_ptr_val(), ty: \"i64\", had_error: false, error_message: \"\" }\n    }\n    .Node(pattern, body, next) -> {\n        let arm_bb = new_bb(ctx, \"march_arm\")\n        let next_bb = new_bb(ctx, \"march_next\")\n        match pattern {\n            .Wildcard -> forge_llvm_build_br(ctx.builder, arm_bb)\n            .Variant(vname, _) -> {\n                let v = variant_lookup(variants, vname)\n                if !v.found { return err_emit(\"pattern references unknown variant `\" + vname + \"`\") }\n                let want_tag = const_i8(ctx, v.tag)\n                let cmp = forge_llvm_build_icmp(ctx.builder, 32, tag_val, want_tag, \"tag_eq\")\n                forge_llvm_build_cond_br(ctx.builder, cmp, arm_bb, next_bb)\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAnd from parse/mod.fg (lines 61-71):\n```forge\nfn expr_is_ident(e: Expr) -> bool {\n    match e {\n        .Ident(_) -> true\n        _ -> false\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- `.VariantName` syntax for pattern matching\n- `.VariantName(arg1, arg2)` for capturing payloads\n- `_` as wildcard\n- `.End` and `.Node(...)` for linked-list style ADTs\n- Nested `match` statements inside match arms\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Real Usage\n\nThe bootstrap compiler demonstrates:\n\n1. **break**: Used in preprocessing loop to exit when newline found\n2. **Field mutation**: `parser.field = value` inside impl methods, saving/restoring parser state\n3. **Nested if-else**: Multiple sequential `if` checks, with early `return`, creating chains\n4. **Multi-arg calls**: Heavy use of 3-4 arg functions like `forge_llvm_function_type()`, `forge_llvm_build_*()`, and `forge_llvm_type_array_set()`\n5. **substring**: Widely used for string slicing, always with `(start, end)` indices\n6. **Enum match**: Both simple variants (`.End`, `.Node`) and parameterized variants (`.Variant(name, params)`) with nested matching and wildcards"}],"totalDurationMs":49554,"totalTokens":134855,"totalToolUseCount":19,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3142,"cache_read_input_tokens":129762,"output_tokens":1944,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3142},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
